  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p>A Bryar Pistol is a cut-down version of a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bryar_Rifle\" title=\"Bryar Rifle\">Bryar Rifle</a>. Though it has less <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a> than the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bryar_Rifle\" title=\"Bryar Rifle\">Bryar Rifle</a> (using standard Pistol <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ranges\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ranges\">Ranges</a>) and deals slightly less damage, the Bryar Pistol is actually more manageable and accurate at Short <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a> than the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bryar_Rifle\" title=\"Bryar Rifle\">Bryar Rifle</a>. </p><p>As a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>, you can prime a Bryar Pistol for a built-up shot. If you make no attacks with the Bryar Pistol before the start of your next turn, the next attack you make before the end of the encounter deals +1 die of damage and consumes 5 charges. </p><p>You may not use any ability that consumes more than one shot (such as <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Autofire\" title=\"Autofire\">Autofire</a> or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Rapid_Shot\" title=\"Rapid Shot\">Rapid Shot</a>) in conjunction with a primed shot. A Bryar Pistol requires a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>&nbsp;to operate. After 100 shots, the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>&nbsp;must be recharged. </p><p><b>Accurate:</b> This weapon takes no penalty when firing at targets at Short&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p>",
